The time zone data files in `chrono-tz/tz/` are sourced from the IANA Time Zone
Database (https://www.iana.org/time-zones, https://github.com/eggert/tz) and
are in the public domain.

Modifications
=============
This fork includes the following changes relative to `chrono-tz` 0.10.4 /
`chrono-tz-build` 0.5.0 / `parse-zoneinfo` 0.4.0:

- Upstream improvements cherry-picked from `chronotope/chrono-tz`:
  - `chrono-tz#211` (Robert Bastian): `%z` numeric offset format support in
    `parse-zoneinfo` (where public `Format::format` takes three arguments as in
    `parse-zoneinfo 0.5.0`, vs two in `0.4.0`), adapted to preserve `%z`
    provenance (`None` in `OffsetName::abbreviation()`) for `chrono-tz 0.10.4`
    runtime parity
  - `chrono-tz#214` (Robert Bastian): link deduplication in `chrono-tz-build`
  - `chrono-tz#218` (Robert Bastian): `CHRONO_TZ_TIMEZONE_FILTER` regex
    filtering (`chrono-tz#215`) selecting only zones whose names match the regex
    (whole-name matching requires anchors such as `^...$`, and an unset or
    blank filter leaves all zones enabled), with conditional `Default for Tz`
    when `UTC` is included and empty-match rejection at build time
  - `chrono-tz#222` (Dirkjan Ochtman): lifetime elision warning cleanups in
    `parse-zoneinfo`
  - `chrono-tz#223` (Yotam Ofek): update `phf` / `phf_codegen` / `phf_shared`
    to `0.13`
  - `chrono-tz#224` (Yotam Ofek): depend on `serde_core` instead of `serde`
  - `chrono-tz#225` (Yotam Ofek): bump MSRV to Rust 1.66.0 across all crates
  - `chrono-tz#226` (Paul Bender): feature-gated `defmt` (`1.0.1`) support
    (requires Rust `1.81+`)
  - `chrono-tz#227` (Paul Bender): clippy warning fixes in `chrono-tz-build`
- IANA Time Zone Database updated from `2025b` to `2026f`
- Security and robustness fixes by the Sadco Security Team:
  - `sad-parse-zoneinfo`: constant-time `i128` Gregorian year-to-timestamp
    calculation clamping `ChangeTime::to_timestamp()` once to `i64`; single-clamp
    `i128` arithmetic in `RuleInfo::absolute_datetime` (including its fallback);
    `1..=31` day token validation plus month/leap-year ordinal and `weekday<=`/`>=`
    validation (`zic`-aligned `Feb weekday<=29` common-year normalization) while
    preserving valid spillover; `i16`/`i128` calendar boundary math;
    `FailedYearParse` on symbolic `Zone` `UNTIL` years and non-panicking
    handling in `RuleInfo` / `ChangeTime`; `TimeSpec` validation allowing leading
    `+`/`-` on hours and rejecting mixed signs or mins/secs `>= 60`; cycle-safe
    `Table::get_zoneset` returning `None` on broken/cyclic links and zone/link
    collision rejection in `TableBuilder`; safe `%z` formatting, template- and
    output-bounded `Format::try_format` (`256`-byte template cap), and fallible
    `Format::try_format_constant`; bounded `Table::try_timespans` /
    `try_codegen_timespans` (`1_024` segments/zone, `4_096` rules/ruleset, `256`
    active/year, `500_000` rule evaluations/zone, `10_000` transitions/zone,
    `64`-byte names), per-year rule base timestamp precomputation, `i128` `UNTIL`
    ordering (`TimestampOutOfRange`) and terminal/monotonic `UNTIL` validation;
    inline `#` comment `break` fix; and safe handling of `>= 4`-segment zone
    names in `structure.rs`
  - `sad-chrono-tz-build`: Rust identifier grammar validation, reserved
    generator declaration/import checks (`IANA_TZDB_VERSION`, `Tz`, `ParseError`,
    `TZ_VARIANTS`, `TIMEZONES`, `MAX_TZ_NAME_LEN`, etc.), normalization/case/
    zone-link collision detection, broken/cyclic link rejection, rejection of
    hierarchies deeper than three segments, empty-selection rejection, `%z`
    provenance preservation, `i32` and `|offset| < 86_400` validation, `{:?}`
    string-literal escaping, `MAX_TZ_NAME_LEN` pre-checks before PHF lookups,
    and in-memory generation before sequential output writes (validation errors
    detected before writing starts leave no files written)
  - `sad-chrono-tz`: single-clamp `i128` arithmetic in
    `FixedTimespanSet::local_span`, `MAX_TZ_NAME_LEN` pre-check in
    `FromStr`/`from_str_insensitive`, `escape_debug()` + `128`-byte UTF-8-safe
    reflected diagnostic budget in `SerdeError`, and dependency on
    `sad-chrono 0.4` (`0.4.48+`)
- Packaging and governance:
  - Published as `sad-chrono-tz` (`0.10.5`, library `sad_chrono_tz`),
    `sad-chrono-tz-build` (`0.5.1`, library `sad_chrono_tz_build`), and
    `sad-parse-zoneinfo` (`0.5.1`, library `sad_parse_zoneinfo`)
  - Real `LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-APACHE` files replacing symlinks

In `sad-chrono-tz` 0.11.0 / `sad-chrono-tz-build` 0.6.0 / `sad-parse-zoneinfo`
0.6.0, the following additional modifications were made:

- Upgraded target dependency to `sad-chrono 0.5` (`0.5.1+`), updated `phf`,
  `phf_codegen`, and `phf_shared` to `0.14`, `defmt` to `1.2`, and `arbitrary`
  to `1.4+`, and raised the MSRV to Rust `1.85.0` across all three crates
- Implemented `core::error::Error` for `ParseError` independently of `std` so
  `#![no_std]` callers receive `Error` without enabling `std`, while `std`
  still controls `#![cfg_attr(not(any(feature = "std", test)), no_std)]`
- Regenerated `chrono-tz/src/prebuilt/{directory,timezones}.rs` with
  `phf_codegen 0.14` and the updated `core::error::Error` impl while keeping
  `chrono-tz 0.10.4`'s verified runtime API surface and IANA tzdb `2026f`

